  stands; each step writes into the draft as it is picked, like every other editor in this popup,
  so there is nothing to accept at the end of one — and still nothing is written to the repo
  until the disk.

The when-line no longer repeats the stage and the importance as words. The toggle row shows both,
live, directly beneath it.

### The quick row, and the chevron

**One row of icons directly under the when, carrying everything small the entry holds**: `24h`,
the stage, `!`, the category, the repetition and the alerts — six icons, no names, one line at
320px. Six named rows are most of a phone screen, and the popup is opened to read an entry far
more often than to fill one in.

Location, participants and details are **not** in it. A pin standing in for an address says only
that there is one, which is what a row of icons is for and what those three are not; they are
lines whether the chevron is open or shut.

**A tap on an icon is the tap on its row.** All-day and important flip where they stand, the
stage cycles, and the category, the repetition and the alerts open exactly the popup their line
opens — anchored under the icon that was tapped. So the chevron changes what is written down,
never what anything does.

**The chevron at the end of the row shows the names**, as lines beneath it, in the order the
icons are in: `24h` and `!` as two chips on one line, then the stage reading `Todo`, `Doing` or
`Done`, then the category, the repetition and the alerts. The icons stay above them — a field
having two ways in is already true of a grid line and a kanban card, and the row is where the
chevron lives. **It is remembered per device**, like the board's orientation: someone who wants
the names wants them every time. It is both the way out and the way back in, which is the rule
every switch in Mine holds to.

**The two toggles and the stage are not fields with an editor each**: they are small values,
edited where they stand with a single tap, and each **shows its value** rather than merely
whether it has one. A tap is the whole edit, into the draft like everything else — there is
nothing in these three to type, so there is nothing for a row's `x` to put back and no editor to
open. The disk appears on the first tap, as it does for any other change.

- **`24h` for all-day** — the one control in the popup that is a word rather than a picture, and
  deliberately so: every drawing of a whole day reads as something else. The sun it replaces was
  taken for weather or for daylight hours, and `24h` cannot be. **A clickable control, not a
  checkbox** — lit when on, plain when off. On an event it is alone on the row. Only the button
  changes its name: the strip in the week and day grids still reads `all-day`, and so does this
  document, because the word is the clearer one in prose and the button is the one place with no
  room for it.
- a **ticked square with the tick knocked out** for **stage** — cycles `todo` → `doing` → `done`
  on each tap, drawn in that stage's kanban colour: red, yellow, green. It is the type marker's
  ticked square *filled in*, so colour and fill tell the two apart rather than a second drawing;
  the badge it replaces was a 9px dot on a 16px corner carrying the one thing the icon can carry
  itself. There is no stage popup — a list of three would be a second way to set one value — and
  its line under the chevron reads the word and cycles too.
- a `!` for **important** — a straight toggle, lit when the task is important and plain when it
  is not. It carries no badge: a yes or no has nothing a badge could add that the lit state has
  not already said, which is what made the old flag need a digit and this one not.

On an event the stage is not there at all, because an event has none. `24h` and `!` are on every
entry, and the stage sits here so that a task that is not on a board still carries what a kanban
  await ev(`document.querySelector('.day .num').click()`);
  await sleep(350);
};

// Each row as label plus background, and - where an icon carries a value rather than only a
// subject - the colour that icon is drawn in: the stage's own, the category's own. That colour
// replaced a badge on a 16px corner and is read the same way, in square brackets.
const row = sel => `[...document.querySelectorAll('${sel} .ib')].map(b => {
  const cs = getComputedStyle(b), svg = b.querySelector('svg');
  const ink = svg ? getComputedStyle(svg).color : '';
  return (b.getAttribute('aria-label') || '?').split(':')[0] +
    (ink && ink !== cs.color ? '[' + ink + ']' : '') +
    (cs.backgroundColor === 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)' ? '' : '@' + cs.backgroundColor);
})`;
const ROW = row('#f-icons'), FLAGS = row('#f-rows .quick');
// Icons alone is a rule about the icon row. The toggle row carries two words on purpose - `24h`,
// because every drawing of a whole day reads as something else, and `!` - so scoping this to the
// icon row is what keeps the two rules from cancelling each other out.
const glyphs = `document.querySelectorAll('#f-icons .glyph').length`;
const words = sel => `[...document.querySelectorAll('${sel} .glyph')].map(g => g.textContent)`;
// The `x` owns the rightmost place in every popup. Read from the left edges, so a row that
// reads correctly but was built in the old order cannot pass - counting three buttons would.
const rightmost = sel => ev(`[...document.querySelectorAll('${sel} button')]
  .filter(b => b.getClientRects().length)
  .sort((a, b) => a.getBoundingClientRect().left - b.getBoundingClientRect().left)
  .map(b => (b.getAttribute('aria-label') || '?').split(':')[0])`);
eq('all-day opens at the start date', (await step()).title, 'Start date');
await pickIn('.pick-body', '12');
eq('and goes straight to the end date, skipping the time', (await step()).title, 'End date');
await pickIn('.pick-body', '14');
eq('which is its last step', (await step()).shut, true);
eq('the row then reads two days and no time at all',
  (await whenRow()).some(t => /\d\d:\d\d/.test(t)), false);

await flag(0);
await sleep(200);
eq('and goes plain again', allday.includes('@'), false);

await click(0);                                   // task
await sleep(300);
const asTask = await ev(FLAGS);
eq('a task row gains the stage, and only the stage', asTask.map(label),
  ['All-day', 'Stage', 'Important', 'Category', 'Repeat', 'Alerts', 'Hide the field names']);
eq('and reads 24h and !', await ev(words('#f-rows .quick')), ['24h', '!']);
eq('the field rows do not reshuffle', (await ev(FIELD_ROWS)).map(r => r.field),
  ['group', 'recurrence', 'alerts', 'location', 'participants']);
ok('a new task starts at todo', !!badge(asTask[1]), 'the stage icon carries its colour');
// Nothing on the row opens an editor: there is no estimate to type any more, so a tap on any of
// the three is the whole edit and the popup grows no field popup of its own.
eq('and the three flags on it open nothing', await ev(
  `[...document.querySelectorAll('#f-rows .quick .ib')].slice(0, 3)
    .some(b => b.dataset.field)`), false);

const stages = [];
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) { await flag(1); await sleep(220); stages.push(badge((await ev(FLAGS))[1])); }
ok('stage cycles through three colours', new Set(stages).size === 3, stages.join(' '));
// A ticked square filled with the stage's colour, not three columns with a dot on the corner.
eq('and is drawn as a ticked square with the tick knocked out', await ev(
  `(() => { const p = document.querySelector('#f-rows .quick .ib:nth-child(2) svg path');
    return [p.getAttribute('fill'), p.getAttribute('fill-rule')]; })()`),
  ['currentColor', 'evenodd']);
ok('and returns to where it started', stages[2] === badge(asTask[1]), `${stages[2]} vs ${badge(asTask[1])}`);

const bangs = [];
for (let i = 0; i < 2; i++) { await flag(2); await sleep(220); bangs.push((await ev(FLAGS))[2]); }
ok('important lights when on', bangs[0].includes('@'), bangs[0]);
ok('and not in green', !bangs[0].endsWith('@' + GOOD), `${bangs[0]} must not be the disk's green`);
ok('two taps return it to plain', !bangs[1].includes('@'), bangs[1]);
eq('and its icon carries no colour of its own either way', bangs.map(badge), ['', '']);

await click(1);                                   // back to an event
await sleep(300);
// The stage is a task's and goes with it; important is not, and stays - the thing a filter
// narrows a calendar view down to is what matters, and half of what matters is a meeting.
// grid line and a kanban card.
await expand(true);
const named = await ev(`(() => ({
  rows: [...document.querySelectorAll('#f-rows .frow')].map(r =>
    r.classList.contains('chips') ? 'chips' : r.dataset.field),
  chips: [...document.querySelectorAll('#f-rows .chips .fchip')]
    .map(c => c.getAttribute('aria-label')),
  stage: document.querySelector('#f-rows [data-field="stage"] .ftap').textContent,
  quick: !!document.querySelector('#f-rows .quick')
}))()`);
eq('the chevron shows a line per icon, in the row\'s own order', named.rows,
